<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38550" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōdĭgĭālis</span></b> ,
		e, adj.
		prodigium. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>Unnatural</i>, <i>strange</i>, <i>wonderful</i>, <i>portentous</i>, <i>prodigious</i> (post-class.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">res,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Amm. 25, 10, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">caput,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. in Ruf. 2, 434</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">signa,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Prud. Ham. 467</span></i>
			.—Adverb.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prodigiale canens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 7, 403</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">cometes prodigiale rubens,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Rapt. Pros. 1, 232</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>That averts bad omens</i> (Plautin.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prodigialis Juppiter,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plaut. Am. 2, 2, 107</span></i>
			.—<i>Adv.</i>: <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōdĭgĭā-lĭter</span></b> ,
				<i>unnaturally</i>, <i>in a strange
				manner</i>, <i>prodigiously</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">variare rem unam,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. A.
					P. 29</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">accidere,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Col.
					3, 3, 3</span></i>
			.</div>
